WEBVTT

01:41.629 --> 01:42.880
Engrave it…

01:49.136 --> 01:51.180
Engrave it upon your body.

01:58.479 --> 02:00.606
Engrave it upon the land.

02:06.570 --> 02:08.823
Engrave it upon the sea.

02:13.869 --> 02:16.163
Engrave it upon your enemy.

02:16.789 --> 02:18.666
Engrave it upon your loot.

02:21.418 --> 02:22.753
Engrave it…

02:23.754 --> 02:25.673
Engrave it…

02:42.106 --> 02:45.150
Engrave your warmth upon me.

03:08.507 --> 03:09.550
Einar!

03:14.221 --> 03:15.347
What was that for!

03:15.431 --> 03:17.349
Right back at you.

03:18.225 --> 03:20.853
If you cut that tree
it'll crush our house.

03:22.605 --> 03:26.358
-Are you going to become a woodcutter?
-No, I'm not.

03:26.442 --> 03:30.112
I'm training for battle!
Take a look at my power!

03:31.280 --> 03:32.990
You may be well-built,

03:33.073 --> 03:36.577
but that doesn't mean you can fight.
Now get the food ready!

03:36.660 --> 03:38.996
I'm starving!

03:43.167 --> 03:45.211
More like, don't throw a knife at me.

03:45.294 --> 03:47.796
Pick something else like plates or spoons.

03:47.880 --> 03:49.506
It's okay if it's a plate?

03:54.762 --> 03:57.723
So that's why bears do it.

03:57.806 --> 03:59.808
-Eat a lot before winter.
-Is that so.

04:05.105 --> 04:07.066
-Thanks.
-So, why did you?

04:07.149 --> 04:08.901
Start training all of a sudden?

04:10.444 --> 04:13.697
What else is there,
other than to protect this place.

04:17.117 --> 04:18.911
Everything was reduced to ashes.

04:19.495 --> 04:21.664
But we finally got back on our feet.

04:23.540 --> 04:26.043
Nobody wants to go through that again.

04:28.337 --> 04:29.797
Even Dad--

04:31.590 --> 04:34.051
Guttorm's milk is delicious!

04:34.134 --> 04:36.971
I know, right? That man knows

04:37.054 --> 04:39.306
how to handle teats.

04:39.390 --> 04:41.433
What's with those fingers? How creepy!

04:41.517 --> 04:42.518
I'm talking here!

04:43.102 --> 04:45.062
-Ew!
-Don't think about it.

04:45.145 --> 04:46.772
Don't involve yourself with warriors.

04:49.441 --> 04:52.736
Aren't you frustrated with
being on the losing end all the time?

04:52.820 --> 04:55.990
Dad died to protect us, you know.

04:56.073 --> 04:58.993
That's right. And that's why you're alive.

04:59.076 --> 05:00.619
You rebuilt the village

05:00.703 --> 05:03.205
and are eating a delicious meal
with two beauties.

05:08.002 --> 05:09.420
We haven't lost.

05:58.510 --> 06:01.388
Listen, once you enter the forest,
just run for your life.

06:01.472 --> 06:02.306
Follow the river…

06:03.599 --> 06:04.808
Róta…

06:05.809 --> 06:06.643
Mom…

06:17.029 --> 06:19.823
Don't think about anything.
Just run straight ahead.

06:20.824 --> 06:22.743
Your brother and mother are with you.

06:58.862 --> 07:00.072
Mom!

07:09.164 --> 07:10.916
Ready? I'll lift you up.

07:14.211 --> 07:15.712
Mom!

07:24.513 --> 07:26.849
Einar, run away.

07:27.724 --> 07:31.019
-Leave me behind.
-Don't be stupid!

07:32.438 --> 07:34.982
Forget that! Just try to stand up!

07:35.065 --> 07:35.983
Mom?

07:36.900 --> 07:38.235
Mom!

07:45.951 --> 07:47.286
Mom!

07:50.497 --> 07:51.790
Stupid girl…

07:54.418 --> 07:57.463
Hey, there are still people over there.

07:58.088 --> 08:01.467
Oh, I see a woman too. Here we come!

08:14.313 --> 08:15.856
Stand up, Einar.

08:17.649 --> 08:19.902
Take Róta… Hurry!

08:21.695 --> 08:22.738
Mom…

08:25.908 --> 08:27.659
I may be a dying old lady…

08:28.535 --> 08:29.703
but I can do this much.

08:31.955 --> 08:33.207
Make it out alive…

08:36.418 --> 08:38.420
As long as you're alive…

08:39.046 --> 08:40.339
you can start again…

08:50.140 --> 08:52.476
Einar…

08:53.894 --> 08:55.062
Róta…

09:15.791 --> 09:17.876
Why aren't they running away?

09:17.960 --> 09:20.379
Hey, she's pretty cute.

09:21.463 --> 09:23.715
Your mama died, right?

09:25.467 --> 09:27.386
-Róta!
-Let go!

09:27.469 --> 09:29.012
-Einar!
-Róta!

09:29.638 --> 09:31.181
Let go of her!

09:32.766 --> 09:34.142
Einar!

09:35.269 --> 09:36.895
I won't forgive you! How dare you!

09:38.397 --> 09:41.358
-Einar!
-How sad.

09:50.951 --> 09:52.327
How dare you--

10:02.713 --> 10:05.549
Hey! What are you doing?!

10:06.133 --> 10:08.260
She stabbed me with something!

10:09.344 --> 10:10.512
What a waste.

10:10.596 --> 10:14.558
Oh well. Let's sell this kid
and get some drinks with that money.

10:15.309 --> 10:17.853
-You're such an idiot!
-I'm sorry, okay?

10:18.478 --> 10:21.189
Come on, drink money.

11:19.373 --> 11:21.583
A FIR TREE STANDING ON BARREN LAND DIES
WITH NO BARK NOR LEAVES TO SHELTER IT

11:21.666 --> 11:23.710
SO IS A MAN WHOM NO ONE LOVES

11:23.794 --> 11:26.338
WHY SHOULD HE KEEP ON LIVING?
EXCERPT FROM HÁVAMÁL

12:08.422 --> 12:09.339
How is she?

12:12.717 --> 12:14.344
This is no good.

12:15.178 --> 12:16.346
Damn it.

12:16.430 --> 12:18.473
We have no choice. Help me carry her.

12:30.902 --> 12:32.654
Ready…

12:34.865 --> 12:36.324
Hey!

12:46.877 --> 12:49.171
Hey! What are you doing?!

12:49.254 --> 12:50.839
You didn't have to throw her out!

12:55.969 --> 12:58.096
Good, it's not inflamed.

13:00.640 --> 13:04.561
We'll pass out fur blankets.
Keep your bodies warm.

13:05.228 --> 13:07.689
We spent a fortune on you all.

13:07.772 --> 13:10.567
Don't you dare become sick
without our approval.

13:11.526 --> 13:15.071
At least stay healthy
until we find a buyer for you. Got that?

13:18.700 --> 13:21.620
Hurry up! We have to furl the sail!

13:49.564 --> 13:50.482
That's right…

13:51.775 --> 13:53.068
I have to live…

14:03.912 --> 14:07.749
Make sure to drink alcohol.
It'll give you a healthy complexion.

14:08.458 --> 14:11.503
Wash every nook and cranny.
Especially your hair.

14:12.295 --> 14:14.381
Get rid of each other's lice.

14:18.885 --> 14:21.596
How is that?

14:22.389 --> 14:26.852
Her hair is fine.
Do her makeup so she looks younger.

14:41.408 --> 14:44.786
How about it? We have
a pretty good lineup, don't we?

14:45.453 --> 14:47.205
They're all so-so.

14:47.289 --> 14:51.209
Don't say that.
We have the best of the best.

14:54.337 --> 14:57.465
That's right… I can't just stay there!

14:58.174 --> 15:01.803
If I can get out of here alive,
I can start again…

15:24.618 --> 15:26.244
Up we go…

15:28.997 --> 15:30.540
A thief!

15:31.416 --> 15:32.792
Sorry!

15:39.507 --> 15:40.675
Hey, Einar.

15:41.760 --> 15:44.679
It seems like you still don't get it.

15:52.103 --> 15:56.149
All right, you slaves. Listen carefully.

15:56.858 --> 15:59.694
Your homelands are far, far away.

15:59.778 --> 16:02.197
You can't return even if you try.

16:02.280 --> 16:06.910
And of course,
no one will help you run away.

16:07.535 --> 16:11.831
That's because you're foreign, penniless,

16:12.415 --> 16:14.084
slaves!

16:14.167 --> 16:17.837
Get someone nice to buy you
and do your best to serve them.

16:18.672 --> 16:22.592
You'll get to eat nice meals, which you
won't if you escape and become a beggar.

16:22.676 --> 16:26.846
Before you venture out,
think about which life is more favorable.

16:28.139 --> 16:30.392
Got that, Einar?

16:45.490 --> 16:46.574
I…

16:48.118 --> 16:49.202
will…

16:50.829 --> 16:51.997
…live!

16:59.087 --> 17:00.672
Yeah…

17:01.339 --> 17:03.174
He's not bad,

17:03.258 --> 17:05.885
but don't you have one with a cuter face?

17:05.969 --> 17:08.471
I see! If that's the case,

17:08.555 --> 17:11.266
I have a special one just for you.

17:11.349 --> 17:14.269
Is that so? How exciting.

17:14.352 --> 17:17.230
I'm sure you will love it.

17:22.861 --> 17:24.529
They are right.

17:25.613 --> 17:26.948
Even if I recklessly escape

17:27.699 --> 17:29.284
I won't have anyone to help me.

17:30.994 --> 17:32.037
Besides…

17:35.498 --> 17:36.374
I don't…

17:37.584 --> 17:40.462
have anywhere to go anymore.

17:42.589 --> 17:43.590
If I just…

17:45.050 --> 17:47.469
give in and become an obedient pet…

17:49.721 --> 17:53.266
My goodness, you sure are lucky.

17:53.349 --> 17:55.518
We just restocked a bunch of them.

17:55.602 --> 17:57.020
Look, that's him.

17:59.230 --> 18:01.399
He's what you're looking for, right?

18:27.926 --> 18:30.553
He's completely different!

18:30.637 --> 18:32.847
He's neither blond nor small!

18:32.931 --> 18:35.975
How weird…
Now that I take a good look, he's not.

18:36.559 --> 18:39.062
Well, anyhow, what do you think about him?

18:39.145 --> 18:41.481
He's strong and sturdy. If you buy now--

18:41.564 --> 18:45.860
Like I said, I'm not here to buy a worker!

18:46.486 --> 18:49.072
I just want to free a relative of mine.

18:49.155 --> 18:52.742
I'm pretty sure he ended up in this town.

18:52.826 --> 18:56.371
He's blond and small
and his name is Thorfinn.

18:56.454 --> 18:59.249
Are you sure you have no clue where he is?

19:07.048 --> 19:08.299
Sorry about that.

19:11.261 --> 19:12.512
Sorry to waste your time.

19:12.595 --> 19:15.515
No worries. Please come again.

19:17.976 --> 19:19.769
He'll never find him.

19:22.856 --> 19:27.110
So he's asking around
in search of his relative, huh?

19:30.989 --> 19:33.491
Whoever has someone like that
searching for him

19:34.033 --> 19:35.410
is so fortunate.

19:40.290 --> 19:41.624
You there.

19:46.379 --> 19:49.716
Can you understand me? Show me your teeth.

20:03.271 --> 20:06.816
-What's your name?
-It's Einar.

20:06.900 --> 20:09.110
Where are you from
and what was your profession?

20:09.694 --> 20:12.071
I was a farmer in the north of England.

20:22.415 --> 20:26.336
Einar, what do you think about
helping out with my field?

20:34.594 --> 20:35.929
Field?

20:59.202 --> 21:01.454
Einar, this way!

21:05.833 --> 21:08.002
All of my servants are working now.

21:08.086 --> 21:11.923
-I'll introduce you during dinnertime.
-Yes, sir.

21:13.549 --> 21:16.010
First, take a look at my farm.

21:47.750 --> 21:52.171
Hey, Mom, are you sure?

21:54.674 --> 21:57.677
I don't even have the freedom to choose

21:57.760 --> 21:59.804
life or death anymore.

22:01.431 --> 22:02.890
Can you still say

22:04.392 --> 22:06.311
that we haven't lost?

22:30.501 --> 22:31.961
My family was killed

22:32.628 --> 22:36.090
and I lost everything
including my homeland.

22:37.800 --> 22:39.343
I didn't even know

22:40.178 --> 22:42.013
what I was living for.

22:50.938 --> 22:54.233
Thorfinn! It's me! Can you come out?

23:10.625 --> 23:12.543
I must be bought by a kind master

23:13.711 --> 23:15.922
and do my very best to serve him.

23:17.590 --> 23:21.385
As long as I stay obedient,
I won't go hungry.

23:22.804 --> 23:25.807
I was starting to believe that.

23:26.307 --> 23:28.142
Thorfinn?

23:39.987 --> 23:40.905
In any case,

23:43.324 --> 23:48.204
that was when I met Thorfinn
for the first time.

25:37.730 --> 25:39.106
"Ketil's farm."

25:39.190 --> 25:40.942
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
